  "prefLabel": "Rev 2906.12 Time Period For Record Retention",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 2906.12 Time Period For Record Retention. The records and information to be retained under this Part shall be retained for:\n\n(a) A period of 3 years from the due date of the return or date filed, whichever is later, unless the retention of the data is required for a longer period of time as a result of:\n\n(1) An extension of the statute of limitations on the assessment of taxes;\n\n(2) The commencement of an adjudicative proceeding involving the parties; or\n\n(3) The completion of any litigation in which the data may be relevant; and\n\n(b) The specific period required under the statute or rule pertaining to a tax administered by the department, if longer than the period specified in (a) above.\n\nSource. #8389, eff 7-8-05; ss by #10388, eff 7-25-13; ss by #13660, eff 6-21-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev2900.html"
